from sagemaker.sklearn.model import SKLearnModel

model = SKLearnModel(

    model_data="s3://insurance-prediction-bucket/insurance-data/output/sagemaker-scikit-learn-2025-05-02-15-20-40-817/output/model.tar.gz",  # <- from training

    role=role,

    entry_point="inference.py",                         # ✅ NEW inference script

    framework_version="1.2-1",

    py_version="py3",

    sagemaker_session=session

)

============

your previous code trained and saved the model; this code takes that saved model and connects it with inference.py, preparing it for deployment and real-time predictions.

========

| Code                                               | Meaning                                                                    |
| -------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `from sagemaker.sklearn.model import SKLearnModel` | Imports the SageMaker class used to create a deployable Scikit-learn model |
| `SKLearnModel()`                                   | Creates a SageMaker model from your trained model files                    |
| `model_data`                                       | Location of your trained `model.tar.gz` file in S3                         |
| `role=role`                                        | IAM role that gives SageMaker permission to access S3 and deploy resources |
| `entry_point="inference.py"`                       | Python file containing the prediction/inference logic                      |
| `framework_version="1.2-1"`                        | Uses Scikit-learn version 1.2-1                                            |
| `py_version="py3"`                                 | Uses Python 3                                                              |
| `sagemaker_session=session`                        | Connects the model operation with your SageMaker session                   |

=====

1. model_data
model_data="s3://insurance-prediction-bucket/.../model.tar.gz"

This is the trained model produced by your previous training job.

train.py
   │
   ▼
SageMaker Training
   │
   ▼
model.tar.gz
   │
   ▼
Amazon S3


2. entry_point="inference.py"

This is a new script used after training.

Your two Python files have different jobs:

===

| File           | Purpose                                       |
| -------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| `train.py`     | Trains the machine learning model             |
| `inference.py` | Loads the trained model and makes predictions |


